WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.840
Over the years, series finales have become
more than just the end of a TV show.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.980
Now, they're bona fide cultural phenomenona,
leaving fans talking for years.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:14.860
Let's take a look at some of the greatest
final episodes of all time.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:18.140
And fair warning, we plan to totally spoil
the ending!

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:19.780
Six Feet Under

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:26.760
HBO's Six Feet Under blended quirky and poignant
elements as well as any series in recent memory,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.820
so it isn't surprising that its finale was
a little bit of both.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:37.240
Fans of the Fisher family watched in stunned
silence as youngest sibling Claire left California

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:38.800
for a job in New York.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.420
As the desert scenery flashed past her window,
we saw flashes of the future for the rest

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:44.780
of the main characters.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.610
In typical Six Feet Under style, we got a
glimpse of what happens to the whole Fisher

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:54.300
family, including how they all age and die,
one by one.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.440
If you're not crying by the end of this one,
you're already dead inside.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.000
Star Trek: The Next Generation

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:06.799
Entitled 'All Good Things', the final Star
Trek: The Next Generation episode marked the

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:10.880
end of seven great seasons of highly acclaimed
television.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:16.249
The series frequently explored social, ethical,
and philosophical issues as the crew probed

00:01:16.249 --> 00:01:19.500
the depths of space, and the finale was no
exception.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:24.800
Captain Picard finds his mind jumping through
three points in the same timeline, forcing

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:30.060
him to think outside of the known laws of
physics to solve the anomaly forced upon him

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:32.919
by the omnipotent, obnoxious being Q.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:34.660
"Not all the Q are alike.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:36.860
Some are almost respectable."

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:42.280
Picard manages to solve the conundrum, returning
to a scene from the series' first episode,

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:47.860
and proving to Q that humanity's potential
is limitless, much to Q's surprise.

00:01:48.109 --> 00:01:52.719
The show ends with a love letter to fans,
as the captain joins a poker game with the

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:54.919
other crew members for the first time.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:57.940
"I should have done this a long time ago."

00:01:58.660 --> 00:01:59.580
Breaking Bad

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:06.620
During its five-year run, Breaking Bad evolved
from just another TV drama into a cultural

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:07.120
phenomenon.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:13.120
When the series finally drew to a close in
2013, fans eagerly anticipated an episode

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:18.140
that promised to wrap up an epic saga of crime,
greed, and vengeance.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.400
And the show absolutely delivered.

00:02:20.569 --> 00:02:26.100
Walt returns from hiding and manages to secure
his family's future, exact his revenge, and

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:30.540
save Jesse from captivity before going down
in a blaze of glory.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:35.390
The way the final scene played out was a direct
punch to the gut for fans.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:41.379
As Badfinger's "Baby Blue" plays in the background,
Walt lovingly examines the meth lab Jesse

00:02:41.379 --> 00:02:46.910
was forced to work in, and even as the sirens
approach in the distance, you wonder if he

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:49.060
might make it out alive after all.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:53.080
Until he collapses to the ground, succumbing
to a bullet wound.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.220
Buffy the Vampire Slayer

00:02:55.860 --> 00:03:01.720
Out of Joss Whedon's many television series,
Buffy the Vampire Slayer is perhaps the most

00:03:01.739 --> 00:03:06.630
beloved, generating legions of fans who still
obsess about the show to this day.

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:11.999
For the finale, Whedon pitted the Scooby Gang
against a malevolent enemy in a battle that

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:18.140
required the characters to work together in
one last showdown in the depths below Sunnydale

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:18.640
High.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:23.879
As you might expect from a show that never
shied away from mortality, not everyone makes

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:24.520
it out alive.

00:03:25.049 --> 00:03:29.960
After the survivors flee from the wreckage
in a school bus, Dawn poses the question many

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:32.920
fans were asking as the credits rolled:

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:34.240
"Yeah, Buffy.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.220
What are we gonna do now?"

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.380
Friday Night Lights

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:46.560
NBC's high school football drama Friday Night
Lights was always more about the cast of characters

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:47.900
than the sport itself.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:53.020
Appropriately enough, when millions tuned
into the finale, they were treated to an episode

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:57.970
that focused on the lives of the characters
long after the last pass was thrown and the

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:00.060
cheers of the crowd faded away.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:04.980
With the state championship in the past, the
characters are shown in the future, with many

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.980
storylines neatly wrapped up.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:11.760
Most importantly, Coach Taylor finally got
to move on, building a new life for himself

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.580
with his wife in Philadelphia.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:15.240
"You ready to go home?"

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:20.220
"Yeah, let's go."

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:23.620
Sons of Anarchy

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:30.190
From 2008 to 2014, Sons of Anarchy lit up
our screens with its high-powered, intense

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:35.560
crime drama chronicling the lives of Jax Teller,
his extended family, and the other members

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:37.200
of the SAMCRO biker club.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:42.490
The final installment of this often bloody,
always exciting modern Shakespearean tragedy

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:45.900
was just as bloody and tragic as the rest
of the series.

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:51.860
Jax eluded police on a high-speed chase until
deliberately driving into the path of an oncoming

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:53.520
semi, ending his own life.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:59.400
While many fans praised his decision as a
selfless way of saving his children's future,

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.950
Jax still managed to be completely selfish
in the end.

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:07.000
Just think of that poor truck driver, probably
scarred for life by the incident.

